  "notes": "Balrampur Chini Mills Ltd (NSE: BALRAMCHIN) \u2014 one of India's largest integrated sugar manufacturers, operating 10 sugar mills in Uttar Pradesh with combined cane crushing capacity ~80,000 TCD. Vertically integrated: sugar + distillery (~1,050 KLPD ethanol capacity, expanding to 1,320 KLPD) + co-generation power. Indian fiscal year ends March 31 (Sugar Season runs Oct\u2013Sep, doesn't match FY). All values in INR millions (1 INR crore = INR 10 million). Source: annual reports filed with BSE/NSE, IR presentations on chini.com. Sector: Integrated Farm Operator (cane procurement from ~5 lakh contracted farmers + own sugar/ethanol/power conversion). Heavily exposed to UP State Advised Price (SAP) for cane, central ethanol blending policy (currently 20% target), and sugar diversion caps. FY22-23 strong on ethanol mix; FY24 hit by govt cap on B-heavy/cane-juice diversion; FY25 starting to recover on PSF-grade ethanol prices. Net debt elevated post PLA (PSF) and ethanol capex.",
